,37018,84386,15170,21,2137,1124,31610,379,284,481,82,11,1124,31610,1147,284,1124,37018,84386,15170,19,92,7110,921,4416,11,279,1685,16340,1352,315,279,2086,1555,374,510,59,26056,2359,7,1124,37018,84386,15170,21,2137,481,82,11,1124,37018,84386,15170,19,92,1124,1291,8,284,274,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,90,16,15170,21,2137,481,16,11,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,92,1124,1291,72341,921,785,5106,4621,315,279,2086,1555,374,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,67,62,17,92,284,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,90,16,15170,21,2137,481,16,11,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,92,1124,1291,10699,3593,785,9210,1124,11520,15976,57758,1948,279,1378,5128,374,279,1852,438,279,9210,1948,862,5106,22879,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,67,62,16,11035,8,323,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,67,62,17,11035,568,576,75259,315,279,9210,1948,1378,22879,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,64,11035,8,323,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,65,11035,8,374,2661,553,510,59,26056,9407,1124,15976,284,1124,37018,35702,10374,13233,90,64,92,1124,50853,1124,10374,13233,90,65,3417,90,22957,10374,13233,90,64,52398,63596,10374,13233,90,65,52398,92,7110,921,5338,11,582,12564,279,12756,1985,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,67,62,16,92,1124,50853,1124,10374,13233,90,67,62,17,11035,982,59,26056,10374,13233,90,67,62,16,92,1124,50853,1124,10374,13233,90,67,62,17,92,284,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,2137,1124,37018,90,16,15170,18,2137,481,16,1124,1291,8,1124,50853,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,90,16,15170,21,2137,481,16,11,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,92,1124,1291,8,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,1124,50853,1124,37018,90,16,15170,21,92,488,1124,37018,90,16,15170,18,92,1124,50853,10293,16,8,488,10293,16,8,1124,50853,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,92,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,16,17,92,481,1124,37018,90,16,15170,18,92,481,1124,37018,90,16,15170,19,92,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,16,17,92,481,1124,37018,90,19,15170,16,17,92,481,1124,37018,90,18,15170,16,17,92,284,1124,37018,90,16,481,220,19,481,220,18,15170,16,17,92,284,481,59,37018,90,21,15170,16,17,92,284,481,59,37018,90,16,15170,17,92,7110,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe set of points $(x,y,z)$ that satisfy\n\\[2x = 3y = -z\\]is a line.\n\nThe set of points $(x,y,z)$ that satisfy\n\\[6x = -y = -4z\\]is another line.\n\nFind the angle between these lines, in degrees.\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo find the angle between the two lines given by the equations \\(2x = 3y = -z\\) and \\(6x = -y = -4z\\), we first need to express these lines in parametric form.\n\nStarting with the first line \\(2x = 3y = -z\\), we can set \\(2x = 3y = -z = t\\). Then, we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{t}{2}, \\quad y = \\frac{t}{3}, \\quad z = -t.\\]\nSo, the parametric form of the first line is:\n\\[\\left( \\frac{t}{2}, \\frac{t}{3}, -t \\right) = t \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right).\\]\nThe direction vector of the first line is \\(\\mathbf{d_1} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right)\\).\n\nNext, for the second line \\(6x = -y = -4z\\), we can set \\(6x = -y = -4z = s\\). Then, we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{s}{6}, \\quad y = -s, \\quad z = \\frac{s}{4}.\\]\nSo, the parametric form of the second line is:\n\\[\\left( \\frac{s}{6}, -s, \\frac{s}{4} \\right) = s \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, \\frac{1}{4} \\right).\\]\nThe direction vector of the second line is \\(\\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, \\frac{1}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nThe angle \\(\\theta\\) between the two lines is the same as the angle between their direction vectors \\(\\mathbf{d_1}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{d_2}\\). The cosine of the angle between two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is given by:\n\\[\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{|\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}|}.\\]\nFirst, we compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2}\\):\n\\[\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right) \\cdot \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, \\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot (-1) + (-1) \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{4}{12} - \\frac{3}{12} = \\frac{1 - 4 - 3}{12} = -\\frac{6}{12} = -\\frac{1}{2}.\\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3e319711f6d02b7ec2d57609079aa611dec7833308a0ba97014372b4378b8049"},"seconds":49.57492470741272,"seed":140513042782955050,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the angle between the two lines given by the equations \\(2x = 3y = -z\\) and \\(6x = -y = -4z\\), we need to first express these lines in terms of their direction vectors.\n\nStarting with the first equation \\(2x = 3y = -z\\):\nLet's set \\(2x = 3y = -z = t\\). Then we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{t}{2}, \\quad y = \\frac{t}{3}, \\quad z = -t.\\]\nThus, the parametric form of the first line can be written as:\n\\[(x, y, z) = t \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector for the first line is \\(\\mathbf{d_1} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right)\\).\n\nNext, consider the second equation \\(6x = -y = -4z\\):\nLet's set \\(6x = -y = -4z = s\\). Then we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{s}{6}, \\quad y = -s, \\quad z = -\\frac{s}{4}.\\]\nThus, the parametric form of the second line can be written as:\n\\[(x, y, z) = s \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector for the second line is \\(\\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nTo find the angle \\(\\theta\\) between the two lines, we need to compute the cosine of the angle between their direction vectors \\(\\mathbf{d_1}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{d_2}\\):\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2}}{|\\mathbf{d_1}| |\\mathbf{d_2}|}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right) \\cdot \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot (-1) + (-1) \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right).\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{4}{12} + \\frac{3}{12} = 0.\n\\]\n\nSince the dot product is zero, the cosine of the angle between the vectors is zero, which means the angle \\(\\theta\\) is:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = 0 \\implies \\theta = 90^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the angle between the two lines is \\(\\boxed{90^\\circ}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{90^\\circ}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the angle between the two lines given by the equations \\(2x = 3y = -z\\) and \\(6x = -y = -4z\\), we need to first express these lines in terms of their direction vectors.\n\nStarting with the first equation \\(2x = 3y = -z\\):\nLet's set \\(2x = 3y = -z = t\\). Then we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{t}{2}, \\quad y = \\frac{t}{3}, \\quad z = -t.\\]\nThus, the parametric form of the first line can be written as:\n\\[(x, y, z) = t \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector for the first line is \\(\\mathbf{d_1} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right)\\).\n\nNext, consider the second equation \\(6x = -y = -4z\\):\nLet's set \\(6x = -y = -4z = s\\). Then we have:\n\\[x = \\frac{s}{6}, \\quad y = -s, \\quad z = -\\frac{s}{4}.\\]\nThus, the parametric form of the second line can be written as:\n\\[(x, y, z) = s \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right).\\]\nSo, the direction vector for the second line is \\(\\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nTo find the angle \\(\\theta\\) between the two lines, we need to compute the cosine of the angle between their direction vectors \\(\\mathbf{d_1}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{d_2}\\):\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2}}{|\\mathbf{d_1}| |\\mathbf{d_2}|}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{d_1} \\cdot \\mathbf{d_2} = \\left( \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, -1 \\right) \\cdot \\left( \\frac{1}{6}, -1, -\\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot (-1) + (-1) \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right).\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{12} - \\frac{4}{12} + \\frac{3}{12} = 0.\n\\]\n\nSince the dot product is zero, the cosine of the angle between the vectors is zero, which means the angle \\(\\theta\\) is:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = 0 \\implies \\theta = 90^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the angle between the two lines is \\(\\boxed{90^\\circ}\\).","id":"precalculus:515"}
